<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Legacy backup rules, used on API 23-30 (`android:fullBackupContent`).
    The API 31+ equivalent is data_extraction_rules.xml, and BOTH are needed:
    minSdk is 26 and targetSdk is 36, so each path is live on some device.

    navette_pairing.xml is EncryptedSharedPreferences. Its ciphertext backs up
    happily; its Android Keystore master key does not, because keystore keys
    are non-exportable by design. So a restore or device transfer produces a
    file that can never be decrypted, and every load() and save() throws from
    then on — permanently, since `by lazy` does not memoize a thrown
    initializer. The app degrades to "pairing never works on this device again"
    with no in-app way out.

    Excluding it means a restored device starts with no pairing and shows
    ConnectScreen, which is correct: re-scanning the QR takes seconds, and the
    token is a credential that arguably should not ride a cloud backup anyway.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude
        domain="sharedpref"
        path="navette_pairing.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
